1.34.m:
Beyond Ilāvṛta is the Nīla realm, known by the name Ramyaka.
Beyond Ramyaka is Śveta, renowned as Hiraṇmaya;
and beyond Hiraṇmaya is Śṛṅgavat, known as Kuru.

Extending to the north is the great mountain named Mālyavat,
a thousand yojanas broad, stretching between Nīla and Niṣadha;
in length, it is stated to be thirty-four thousand [yojanas].

Between the two circular ranges stands Meru, the supreme mountain,
four-colored, made of pure gold, four-sided, high-raised.
From the unmanifest all the elements, water and the rest, arose;

The pericarp of that lotus is circular all around;
ninety-six thousand yojanas it is proclaimed,
and eighty-four placed in the intervals.
